  "output": "(1) Bug: `reapOrphanedRuns` defaults `staleThresholdMs` to **0**. Startup calls it with no argument, so `cutoff = Date.now() - 0 = now`.\n\n(2) Why all fail: the check is `lastHeartbeatAt <= cutoff`. Every still-running run has `lastHeartbeatAt <= now`, so all match on a clean restart and `failRun(..., 'process_lost')` with `shouldRetry=false` \u2014 permanent, not resumed.\n\n(3) Fix: pass a non-zero startup grace (e.g. `staleThresholdMs: 60_000`) or raise the default above 0 so live runs have a window to heartbeat; never reap at boot with default 0.",
